### LMS API (server/src/Lms.Api) — run with `dotnet run --project src/Lms.Api`
@lms = http://localhost:5200

### Is ISMS reachable with the configured credentials? (never shows the key)
GET {{lms}}/api/isms/status
Accept: application/json

### All classes (section + subject + instructor offerings) from ISMS schedules
GET {{lms}}/api/classes
Accept: application/json

### Classes filtered by instructor and term
GET {{lms}}/api/classes?instructorId=EMP-7&schoolYearId=2026&semesterId=1
Accept: application/json

### Students in a class — use an "id" from GET /api/classes
@classId = U0NILTEfMTAxH0VNUC03
GET {{lms}}/api/classes/{{classId}}/students
Accept: application/json

### Subjects
GET {{lms}}/api/subjects
Accept: application/json

### Instructors
GET {{lms}}/api/instructors
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{lms}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### CORS preflight from the Vite dev server (allowed in Development)
OPTIONS {{lms}}/api/classes
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET

### Writes are deliberately absent: classes and subjects are owned by ISMS -> 405
POST {{lms}}/api/classes
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### LMS database reachable and migrated, and the result of the last ISMS sync
GET {{lms}}/api/lms/status

### Class content as an instructor (demo identity, Development only).
### Use an ISMS employee id that teaches classes, e.g. from GET /api/instructors.
@instructor = EMP-0003
GET {{lms}}/api/me/classes
X-Demo-User-Id: {{instructor}}
X-Demo-Role: instructor

### Modules of one of those classes (paste a class id from the response above)
@classId = replace-with-a-class-id
GET {{lms}}/api/classes/{{classId}}/modules
X-Demo-User-Id: {{instructor}}
X-Demo-Role: instructor

### Post an announcement
POST {{lms}}/api/classes/{{classId}}/announcements
X-Demo-User-Id: {{instructor}}
X-Demo-Role: instructor
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Lab on Thursday", "message": "Bring your laptops." }

### The same class as a student on its class list
GET {{lms}}/api/classes/{{classId}}/announcements
X-Demo-User-Id: STU-0011
X-Demo-Role: student

### Assignment draft as a student (contract §7): save, add a file, turn in
@assignmentId = replace-with-an-assignment-id
PUT {{lms}}/api/classes/{{classId}}/coursework/{{assignmentId}}/draft
X-Demo-User-Id: STU-0011
X-Demo-Role: student
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "See the attached diagram.", "link": null }

### Add a file to the draft (type decided from the bytes; scanned before it is kept)
POST {{lms}}/api/classes/{{classId}}/coursework/{{assignmentId}}/draft/files
X-Demo-User-Id: STU-0011
X-Demo-Role: student
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=lms

--lms
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Entities: Student, Class, Enrollment.
--lms--

### Turn the draft in; the answer is the receipt
POST {{lms}}/api/classes/{{classId}}/coursework/{{assignmentId}}/draft/turn-in
X-Demo-User-Id: STU-0011
X-Demo-Role: student
Content-Type: application/json

{}
